= What I care about: the rubric
#md("/docs/rubric.md")
== Sources and limits
- Party evidence was gathered on 27 October 2026 by research agents (Claude Sonnet) following `research/BRIEF.md`, from party websites and platforms, the Israel Democracy Institute election pages and the Israeli and international press. Each claim in `research/parties/` is labelled confirmed or inferred and cited.
- Scoring was done in one pass by a single agent (Claude Opus) from that evidence, so every list is graded on the same reading of the rubric. Scores are judgements against Daniel's stated positions, not neutral ratings of the parties.
- Gaps: several party sites refused automated access; some image-only PDFs could not be read; minor lists got a light sweep (2–5 searches each). Where nothing was found, the list scores 0 on that Stream A item. For Daniel's purposes, a policy that can't be found is no policy.
